From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:21:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 077/207] In-model runner: graph first for any pure-integer
 calc program

With TF_DSV41_RUNNER_BACKEND=graph, a fence, REPL or inline cell whose lowered calc program is integer
arithmetic (+ - * // % **, literal exponents, nonzero literal divisors) runs as one packet of T1's bank
plans, each sized from syntax bounds within 62 digits. Everything else stays on calc or ELF.
